This patch fixes pretrained positional conv embedding weights (pos_conv_embed)
silently failing to load under torch versions that provide
nn.utils.parametrizations.weight_norm (torch>=2.1). transformers==4.33.2 has a
forward-compat hasattr() check that opts into the newer parametrizations-based
weight_norm when available, but this transformers version has no matching
state-dict key-renaming logic, so the checkpoint's flat weight_g/weight_v keys
go unused and the module's parametrizations.weight.original0/1 params are
randomly reinitialized instead. Forcing the legacy nn.utils.weight_norm keeps
the module's parameter names matching the checkpoint's, restoring correct
pretrained-weight loading. Verified against transformers==4.33.2 + torch==2.5.1.
Apply this after patches/transformers+4.33.2.patch.
--- a/transformers/models/wavlm/modeling_wavlm.py
+++ b/transformers/models/wavlm/modeling_wavlm.py
@@ -280,9 +280,12 @@
             groups=config.num_conv_pos_embedding_groups,
         )
 
+        # Force legacy weight_norm (not nn.utils.parametrizations.weight_norm) so the
+        # constructed module's parameter names (weight_g/weight_v) match the pretrained
+        # checkpoint's flat key names; this transformers version has no key-renaming
+        # logic for the newer parametrizations-based naming, so using it here would
+        # silently fail to load the pretrained positional conv embedding weights.
         weight_norm = nn.utils.weight_norm
-        if hasattr(nn.utils.parametrizations, "weight_norm"):
-            weight_norm = nn.utils.parametrizations.weight_norm
 
         if is_deepspeed_zero3_enabled():
             import deepspeed
